1
00:00:00,133 --> 00:00:01,733
Your mind has weaknesses

2
00:00:01,733 --> 00:00:04,133
you probably don't even know about.

3
00:00:05,167 --> 00:00:07,733
First, social exclusion:

4
00:00:07,867 --> 00:00:09,367
being ignored can threaten

5
00:00:09,367 --> 00:00:10,967
our sense of belonging.

6
00:00:10,967 --> 00:00:12,767
That feeling can hurt,

7
00:00:12,833 --> 00:00:15,000
even when no one says a word.

8
00:00:15,167 --> 00:00:17,200
Next, mirroring:

9
00:00:17,267 --> 00:00:18,867
people often unconsciously

10
00:00:18,867 --> 00:00:21,267
copy gestures and expressions.

11
00:00:21,267 --> 00:00:22,467
This Chameleon Effect

12
00:00:22,467 --> 00:00:23,567
can help interactions

13
00:00:23,567 --> 00:00:25,067
feel more natural.

14
00:00:25,167 --> 00:00:26,967
Then there's scarcity:

15
00:00:27,067 --> 00:00:28,700
limited availability can make

16
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:30,700
things seem more desirable.

17
00:00:30,700 --> 00:00:31,900
That's why countdowns

18
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:33,300
and 'only a few left'

19
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:35,167
can influence decisions.

20
00:00:35,167 --> 00:00:36,567
The foot-in-the-door effect

21
00:00:36,567 --> 00:00:38,967
starts with a small request.

22
00:00:40,167 --> 00:00:41,600
Agreeing once can make

23
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:42,767
a larger request

24
00:00:42,767 --> 00:00:44,400
easier to accept.

25
00:00:45,133 --> 00:00:46,967
But threaten someone's freedom,

26
00:00:46,967 --> 00:00:49,567
and reactance may make them push back.

27
00:00:49,567 --> 00:00:51,867
Sometimes, controlling your choices

28
00:00:51,867 --> 00:00:54,000
starts by making you feel

29
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:55,367
you have none.

